# Cryoze Engine

A 2D physics engine written in C++ using the SDL3 library for graphics rendering.

Cryoze is a modular simulation framework designed for developers who want to build accurate physics demos and interactive applications without manually developing an engine backend.
Each simulation is a self-contained Scenario, which belongs in a single class


## Features

- Particle dynamics using forces and mass-spring constraints.
- Plane collisions with restitution and friction.
- Fixed-timestep simulation loop using velocity verlet integration for stable, reproducible results.
- (Optional) Scenario selection menu included for code-free control of example simulations.


 ## Example Simulations

*Scenario | Purpose*
Freefall | Demonstrate constant acceleration under gravity and bouncing masses (rebounding.)
Projectile | Demonstrate projectile motion and simulate expected results without use of SUVAT calculations.
Oscillator | Demonstrate damped oscillations in mass-spring systems.